#29603
"Chamber of Comestibles"
"Large black cauldron dominates this chamber placed centrally on the floor. 
Unlike the other chambers, the granite walls have a softer look to them,
likely from build up of soot and other particulate matter over the years. 
Stone shelves are carved into the eastern wall while a solid granite table top
protrudes from the northern wall, making up the cooking surface.
"
""
